 five conservation easements, one oil and gas field restoration project, one conifer \nremoval restoration project, two conifer removal projects, and one road restoration project. Montana Sage Grouse Habitat Conservation \nProgram. “2024 Annual Report”. https://sagegrouse.mt.gov/documents/2024AnnualReport  \n8 Based on data received from Montana Sage Grouse Habitat Conservation Program November 20, 2025. \n9 Montana Sage Grouse Habitat Conservation Program. “2024 Annual Report”. https://sagegrouse.mt.gov/documents/2024AnnualReport  \n10 Based on data received from Montana Sage Grouse Habitat Conservation Program November 20, 2025. \n \nINDUSTRIAL ECONOMICS, INCORPORATED \n \n \n \n \n4--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPublic Notice: Opportunity for public input on 2024 Annual Report: June 23, 2025, 7:00 pm | City of Langley (https://www.langleycity.ca/news/public-notice-opportunity-public-input-2024-annual-report-june-23-2025-700-pm)\nciteturn56search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.4 years ago; Crawled: last month; # Public Notice: Opportunity for public input on 2024 Annual Report: June 23, 2025, 7:00 pm\n\n# Public Notice: Opportunity for public input on 2024 Annual Report: June 23, 2025, 7:00 pm\n\nDate\n\nJune 3, 2025\n\nPursuant to section 98 of the Community Charter, Langley City Council will consider the 2024 Annual Report at the Committee of the Whole during the Regular Council Meeting on Monday, June 23, 2025, at 7:00 pm in Council Chambers at Langley City Hall (20399 Douglas Crescent).\n\nThe Annual Report is a statement of municipal objectives and is used to report our progress respecting those objectives. The report includes: \n\n  * Message from the Mayor and CAO \n  * Your city by the numbers \n  * 2024 community grants \n  * Permissive tax exemptions \n  * Financial statements \n\n### View the 2024 Annual Report \n\n###### Online: LangleyCity.ca/2024AnnualReport\n\n###### In-person: \n\n  * Timms Community Centre, 20399 Douglas Crescent \n  * Langley City Hall Administration and Corporate Services, 20399 Douglas Crescent \n  * Al Anderson Memorial Pool, 4949 207 Street \n  * Langley City Fire Rescue Service, 5785 203 Street \n\nFind hours of operation: LangleyCity.ca/Hours\n\n### Share your opinions\n\nShare your views about the 2024 Annual Report by sending in written submissions to City Council. Your submission must be received no later than 12:00 pm, noon, on Monday, June 23, 2025 and will form part of the public record and may be published in a meeting agenda. \n\n### \nWays to submit your submission: \n\n  1. Email: councilmeetings@langleycity.ca \n\n  2. Mail: ATTN Deputy Corporate Officer, Langley City Hall, 20399 Douglas Crescent, Langley, B.C., V3A 4B3 \n\n### Questions?\n\nContact Paula Kusack, Deputy Corporate Officer, by emailing councilmeetings@langleycity.ca. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInvestor--Shareholders' Meeting-Shareholders' Meeting | Unitech Global | Your Brilliant AIDC Solution Provider (https://www.ute.com/en/ir/shareholder/meeting)\nciteturn56search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month;   * 2024AnnualReport\nImage Shareholders' Meeting | Unitech Global | Your Brilliant AIDC Solution Provider iframe iframe\n\n  * Investor\n\n    * Investor Relations\n    * Shareholders' Meeting\n    * Quarterly Results\n    * Investor News\n\n\n  *   *   *   * Investor Relations\n  * Shareholders' Meeting\n  * Quarterly Results\n  * Investor News\n\n## Shareholders' Meeting\n\n[Select]\n\n  * 2026 Shareholders' Meeting\n\n  * Handbook for the 2026 Annual Meeting of Shareholders\n\n  * Notice for 2026 Annual General Shareholders' Meeting\n\n  * 2025 AnnualReport\n\n  * 2025 Shareholders' Meeting\n\n  * 2025 List of Major Shareholders\n\n  * Handbook for the 2025 Annual Meeting of Shareholders\n\n  * Notice for 2025 Annual General Shareholders' Meeting\n\n  * 2024AnnualReport\n\n  * 2024 Shareholders' Me